# Build output directory

- GN/Ninja **gen roots** are **`out/Debug`** (`is_debug=true`) and **`out/Release`** (`is_debug=false`). Binaries live under those dirs (`out/Debug/build.ninja`, `out/Release/SmartGIS.exe`, …).
- **Do not** use bare **`out/`** as a gen root. **Do not** use **`out/Default`**.
- Default **`build.bat`** builds **both** configs. Prefer a single config when iterating: `build.bat debug …` / `build.bat release …`.
- Shared (not a gen root) — keep `out/` top-level to this set:
  - `out/environment.x64.x64` (copied into each config dir for `ninja -t msvc`)
  - `out/third_party` -> `third_party/.install` junction
  - **`out/data/`** — sample maps / DEM / AM terrain (GN `//testing/data:china_map_samples` writes `$root_out_dir/../data`). **Do not** drop `china_city.*` / `china_dem.tif` on the bare `out/` root.
  - **`out/data/cache/`** — regenerable download caches (`china_city_src/`, `china_dem_src/` for `testing/data/build_china_*.py`)
  - **`out/ui/`** — Views shell/toolkit markup `.ui.xml` / `.ui.css` (GN `//src/ui/views:markup_resources` writes `$root_out_dir/../ui`)
  - **`out/plugins/<package>/`** — product plugin self-managed resources (e.g. `world3d/`); shell `--plugins-dir` defaults to `<exe>/../plugins`
  - **`out/crash/`** — cdb / minidump sessions. **Do not** use repo-root `crash/` (legacy; merged here)
  - **`out/ui_forensics/`** — UI Mode A failure dumps (`<run_id>/`); wipe old runs freely
  - **`out/.build.lock*`** / **`out/.build.waiters/`**, optional **`out/agent_wake_queue.md`** — multi-agent build / wake coordination
- Logs: `out/Debug/build.log`, `out/Release/build.log`.
- **Harness / loop artifacts** (marks, showcase BMP/PNG, `*_loop_report.json`): **`out/<config>/captures/<scenario>/`** — not the gen-root top level. Scenario dirs mirror `testing/tools/harness/<family>/` (`atmosphere/`, `map2d/`, `plugin/`, `ui/`, `legacy/`, `shell/`). Cross-cutting: **`captures/record/`** (HWND mp4 / `*_frames`), **`captures/analysis/<topic>/`** (playback BMP + `playback.json`), **`captures/_scratch/`** (one-shot `_diag*` / `_inspect*`). Agents may wipe old captures freely.
- **Agent scratch** (redirected stdout/stderr, one-shot scripts, `.old` binaries): **`out/<config>/log/`** (text dumps) and **`out/scratch/`** (shared junk). Wipe freely; do not stash these at the gen-root root.
- Resolve product/test binaries under **`out/Debug/`** (default for `te` / `e2e` runners) or **`out/Release/`**.
- Third-party CMake install prefix remains **`out/third_party`** (junction to `.install`). Do not invent a second install root.
- Do not use `vs2008/SmartGIS.sln` as a build entry.
- Do not stash one-shot scripts, recovered sources, or nested `out/Debug/out/` under `out/`. Gen-root top level should stay **binaries + ninja + known subdirs** (`obj/`, `gen/`, `captures/`, `log/`, `plugin/`, `ui/`, `third_party/`, …).

```bat
build.bat
build.bat debug
build.bat release te
gn gen out/Debug --root=./ --args="is_debug=true is_build_third_party=false"
ninja -C out/Debug all
```

## Agent compile

Agents **may** run `build.bat`, `gn`, `ninja`, and `out/Debug|Release/*.exe` when fixing or verifying builds/tests. Prefer repo-root **`build.bat`**. Compile lock is **off by default**; see **`.cursor/rules/build/build-lock.mdc`**. Also **`.cursor/rules/build/agent-may-build.mdc`**. Do not invent `third_party/.install` as a gen root; do not use `SmartGIS.sln` / MSBuild as the fix loop.
